</span><span class=\"n\">Illegal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instruction</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dumped</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This test:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"wasm\"><pre><span></span><code>(module\n  (tag $e (param i32))\n  (func $throw (param i32)\n    local.get 0\n    throw $e)\n  (func (export \"f\") (param i32) (result i32)\n    (block $h (result i32)\n      (try_table (catch $e $h)\n        local.get 0\n        call $throw)\n      unreachable)))\n\n(assert_return (invoke \"f\" (i32.const 5)) (i32.const 5))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">unknown</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">linux</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gnu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Ccranelift</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bti</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">try</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">table</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span>\n<span class=\"n\">qemu</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">uncaught</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">signal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Illegal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instruction</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dumped</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This test:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"wasm\"><pre><span></span><code>(module\n  (type $t (func (param i32) (result i32)))\n  (table funcref (elem $g))\n  (func $g (type $t)\n    local.get 0\n    i32.const 1\n    i32.add)\n  (func (export \"f\") (param i32) (result i32)\n    local.get 0\n    i32.const 0\n    return_call_indirect (type $t)))\n\n(assert_return (invoke \"f\" (i32.const 5)) (i32.const 6))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">unknown</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">linux</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gnu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Ccranelift</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bti</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">call</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">indirect</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span>\n<span class=\"n\">qemu</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">uncaught</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">signal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Illegal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instruction</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dumped</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This test:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"wasm\"><pre><span></span><code>(module\n  (type $t (func (param i32) (result i32)))\n  (table funcref (elem $g))\n  (func $g (type $t)\n    local.get 0\n    i32.const 1\n    i32.add)\n  (func (export \"f\") (param i32) (result i32)\n    local.get 0\n    i32.const 0\n    call_indirect (type $t)))\n\n(assert_return (invoke \"f\" (i32.const 5)) (i32.const 6))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">unknown</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">linux</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gnu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Ccranelift</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">use</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bti</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">Ccranelift</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">sign</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">address</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">call</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">indirect</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wast</span>\n<span class=\"n\">qemu</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">uncaught</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">signal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Illegal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instruction</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dumped</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>&lt;details&gt;<br>\n&lt;summary&gt;LLM summary, if useful&lt;/summary&gt;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>br_table</code> default:</strong> since #14826 the aarch64 jump-table sequence<br>\n  clamps the index and reaches the default block through the table, but<br>\n<code>visit_block_succs</code> (<code>inst_predicates.rs</code>) still reports the default as<br>\n  a direct successor, so it gets no <code>bti j</code>. The expected output in<br>\n<code>filetests/isa/aarch64/bti.clif</code> already shows this.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>try_table</code> handlers:</strong> the unwinder resumes into <code>try_call</code> handler<br>\n  blocks with <code>br x4</code> (<code>crates/unwinder/src/arch/aarch64.rs</code>), but handler<br>\n  blocks aren't treated as indirect-branch targets, so they get no<br>\n<code>bti j</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>return_call_indirect</code> / <code>return_call_ref</code>:</strong> <code>ReturnCallInd</code> pins the<br>\n  target to x1 and emits <code>br x1</code>. The callee's <code>bti c</code> accepts <code>br</code> only<br>\n  from x16/x17.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>call_indirect</code> with <code>sign_return_address</code>:</strong> <code>tail</code>-convention<br>\n  functions sign with the zero-modifier key (<code>paciaz</code>) and skip <code>bti c</code>,<br>\n  assuming the PACI instruction is an implicit landing pad. Only<br>\n<code>paciasp</code>/<code>pacibsp</code> are, so every <code>blr</code> into a Wasm function faults.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>CLIF runtests don't catch any of this: the runner skips a <code>target\n  aarch64 use_bti</code> line because <code>cranelift-native</code> never reports<br>\n<code>use_bti</code> for the host, so <code>runtests/br_table.clif</code>'s existing <code>use_bti</code><br>\n  target never runs.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&lt;/details&gt;<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
